{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The records of the events a tracker tracks, in the order tracked: what a delivery reads."}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/Records-swift.struct\/AsyncIterator"],"generated":true,"title":"Structures"},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/Records-swift.struct\/makeAsyncIterator()"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods"},{"anchor":"Type-Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/Records-swift.struct\/Element","doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/Records-swift.struct\/Failure"],"generated":true,"title":"Type Aliases"},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/Records-swift.struct\/AsyncSequence-Implementations"],"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Records"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let tracker = Tracker()","let delivery = tracker.records","    .batch(strategy: .count(20))","    .deliver(to: ConsoleDestination())"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The sequence ends once the tracker’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/finish()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is called, or its every copy is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"released, and every record before it has been read. Records tracked while nothing is reading wait in memory, with